 { In this apparently drawish position, White decided matters by means of a barrier. } 1. { -KEY- } Kc5 $1 { King first, denying Black's king the d6-square. } ( { The hasty } 1. a5 $2 { would just draw after } Kd6 $1 ( { but not } 1. Kc5 Ne5 $2 2. Kc5 $1 { with similar play to the game } ) 
2. a6 Ne5 { and the knight reaches c6 in time. } ) 
f5 ( { Or } 1... Ne5 2. a5 Nd7 3. Kc6 $1 { and wins - Dvoretsky. } ) 
2. a5 f4 3. a6 f3 4. Nc4 $1 ( { After } 4. a7 $2 f2 5. a8=Q $11 f1=Q $11 6. Qe8 Kf5 { Black escapes. } ) 
f2 5. Nd2 Nf6 6. Kc6 $1 ( { Avoiding the last trap: } 6. a7 $2 Ne4 $1 ) 
Ne4 7. Nf1 
 1-0

