 { The barrier is also frequently used by the defending side. In the above position the bishop outranks the knight, but White has a very simple way of maintaining the balance. } 1. { -KEY- } Nd3 $1 f5 2. f3 Kf7 3. e4 $1 Ke7 4. b3 { The barrier is complete and now prevents the black king from invading White's territory. Neither player can do much, so a draw was agreed. } g6 
